    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d38">

                <pb facs="0134" n="50" xml:id="pg50"/>

                <head>No. 37.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pringle to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1885-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 6, 1885</date>. (Received January 4,
                        1886.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 454.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to report that the elections passed
                    off quietly, and General Manuel Barillas has been elected constitutional
                    President, and Vicente Castaneda Vice-President of the Republic of
                    Guatemala.</p>
                <p>The official announcement does not take place until Congress meets next
                    August.</p>
                <p>I also inclose a decree of General Menendez, President of Salvador, relative to
                    the dissolution of the Assembly, and also the decree in which he declares the
                    country under martial law.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>D. LYNCH PRINGLE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad
                            interim.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d38-a1.xml" xpointer="d38-a1"/>
